  "interpretation": [
    "Exactly 1,000,000 files initially; 999,870 sharing jobs include 999,869 whole files and one partial range. All 1,000,003 final files pass independent byte/inode checks and match a fresh portable full scan.",
    "The FIRST post-apply invocation is required to be idle. Extra settling passes are forbidden by both the driver and output validator.",
    "Successful apply captures 999,870 destination maps and acknowledges their committed inode events without reopening destinations on the next invocation.",
    "Separate hosted runs measured apply plus first follow-up at 200.321 seconds before and 242.868 seconds after. These numbers do not establish an overall throughput improvement.",
    "Unchanged control operations also differed between hosts: initial indexing 251.003 versus 315.074 seconds, and fresh full scan 191.339 versus 234.252 seconds. Do not attribute all timing changes to the patch.",
    "Normal small-change and idle cases use medians of three samples; initial indexing/apply and the representative write are single samples.",
    "Each 4 KiB write in the shared 8 MiB destination hashes one 128 KiB chunk and reuses 63. Source-dependent completion replay remains bounded without reading unchanged contents.",
    "Peak RSS belongs to the actual dedupit CLI, excluding guest kernel page cache, test driver and VM host. Native index size includes allocated SQLite pages, including the freelist.",
    "The exact benchmark source commit and executable digest are retained. Subsequent commits add QEMU power-cut validation and refine crash-test assertions without changing the successful-apply algorithm."
  ]
